                <pb facs="0365" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg353"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94114A/6–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-14">July 14, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2310. Legtel 3448 [<hi rendition="#italic">3348</hi>], June 28. Request FonOff to
                    have Gorgé inform Jap Govt at opportune moment that cultural background of
                    American people is opposed to cremation of American dead and some religious
                    beliefs forbid cremation. It is hoped therefore that American dead will be
                    inhumed whenever possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
